<b>א.</b> For the service of his Creator - for this is what man was created for, as the scripture says: "All that is called by my name and for my honor have been created" etc. And even if Yeshiyan created in the winter to say: How will you get up in the morning, because the cold is great; Or will we rise in the summer to say: How will you get up from your bed, and you are not yet satisfied from your sleep? He will overcome him and not listen to him, and he will think in his soul: if he had to stand and serve before a king of flesh and blood, how careful and quick he would be to stand alert and prepare himself for his work; All the more and the son of the son of the son of the son of the King of Kings, blessed be He.<br>
<br>
<b>ב.</b> Hashahar - Bslah wrote a secret, connecting day and night with Torah or prayer, both in the morning and in the evening. And as soon as he wakes up from his sleep and does not want to sleep, he will take his hands, even if he remains lying down. And even more so that he should not walk four cubits without shaking hands. And you have to be very careful about it. And the holy Zohar sails for this in his punishment to Mars, because he put the spirit of impurity on himself. And in any case, it is forbidden to pass any prohibition for the lack of shaking hands, such as stopping himself from urinating by doing so, or taking water that his friend has prepared for himself, if it is not clear to him that he will immediately give others in exchange for it. And some will fail in this. If it happens that the water is far away and there is no one to bring it closer to him, let some of those with a good heart walk less than four cubits. And the gatekeepers wrote an answer to this, Della Nahira, the more that they should go quickly, so as not to harbor an evil spirit by his hands. Some say in this matter that Amrinan Kole Beta is about four cubits of blood, but this should not be trusted except in times of need. If it happens that he does not have water at night to wash his hands three times in order to pass away the spirit of impurity, nevertheless, Hashem forbid that he should cancel the words of the Torah because of this until the day dawns, but instead he will take a little or clean his hands from all the hands of a demanki and bless and learn, according to the law of the Talmud and the judges.<br>
<br>
<b>ג.</b> For the public to pray - even though there will be no time for prayer, we are in any case a mitzvah with the public. And refer to Lakman at the end of subsection IX.<br>
<br>
<b>ד.</b> The righteous - that is, he should always picture in his mind how he stands before Hashem, blessed be He, because the Almighty fills the whole earth with His glory. And they wrote in the name of the late Hari, that he should draw the name of Hashem always before his eyes in the score of fear, such as Y-H-V-H, and this is the secret of "I will always be with the Lord against me", and this is a great benefit in the matter of fear. And some were accustomed for this reason to make lamps of painted parchment to place in siddurs, and write on them "Shuyti the" and a four-letter letter and the rest of names, and such a menorah would be called "Shuyti". And the reason is so that he will be remembered not to talk about idle conversation in the midst of the fear of Hashem. And he wrote in the gates of Tshuva in the name of the bull grain that it is appropriate for the area to cancel the custom, because according to the majority they do not preserve the parchment properly, and it was spilled at the head of every khutz, and also several times came to the effect of erasing the name. And we will see the large candlesticks painted on parchment that are placed in the synagogue in front of the column under a glass tabla, which does not belong to the above-mentioned taste, lit len ​​ba, so far as the language is concerned. And the kobein on the column without a tabla should be protested with their hand, because by the candles that are kobein on the column, most of the time it comes to the erasure of the name Hass and Shalom.<br>
<br>
<b>ה.</b> From people - and in any case he should not quarrel with them, because the degree of fierceness is very obscene, and it is not appropriate to use it at all, even in the service of Hashem, may Hashem bless him, because he will buy property in his soul to be fierce even if it is not at his place of work, may he be blessed (2i). And refer to the explanation of the halacha.<br>
<br>
<b>ו.</b> Those who mock him - and even if he is a mediocre person standing in the place of great ones, he will not be ashamed of them to learn and do the mitzvah. But if it is possible for him to do the mitzvah without them, better. And who is in the presence of mediums who will learn from him, it must be said, it is better to do in front of them, who will learn from him to do as he did. But let his heart be for the sake of heaven, and not to boast, Hashem forbid.<br>
<br>
<b>ז.</b> Even with austerity go - wants to say, even when he is at home in austerity, so will his departure be with the Lord his Hashem, and as he finishes and goes.<br>
<br>
<b>ח.</b> Quickly - not necessarily, but he should stay a little and not stand up suddenly, because that is harmful to the body [Gitin, p. It is good to say immediately in his wake: "I thank you before the living and existing king that you restored my soul in my compassion, great is your faith." And the box "in compassion" will be in Athanatha, and "great is your faith" without ceasing. And it is from what is written: "New to the mornings" etc., that the Almighty fulfills his belief to return the souls of the entrusted in the morning. And there is no need for the laying on of hands, even if his hands are dirty, because the wording does not mention either a name or a nickname. And from any place to learn it seems Dasor first took his hands, and in the least it is forbidden before the blessing of the Torah. And refer to the end of paragraph 2 above.
